<edge source="global_financial_fragili::currency_pressure_index" target="middle_east_energy_attac::supply_disruption_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained depreciation pressure on an import-dependent economy's currency increases the likelihood that buyers miss payments or suppliers preemptively halt shipments (or require cash-on-delivery), raising the probability and severity of supply interruptions for energy and critical goods.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_fragili</data>
  <data key="d40">middle_east_energy_attac</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_financial_fragili::currency_pressure_index" target="russia_ukraine_war::arms_transfer_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained depreciation pressure on the ruble (or other regional currencies) disrupts FX settlement and raises foreign‑currency costs for overseas procurement and intermediary payments, delaying or reducing the volume of imported munitions and equipment arriving into the theater.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_fragili</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_financial_fragili::currency_pressure_index" target="us_china_tech_trade::ai_infra_investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Appreciable depreciation pressure on the local currency raises the local‑currency cost of imported GPUs, servers and construction inputs (priced in USD), directly worsening project economics and prompting developers and investors to cut or postpone new AI infra capital deployments.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_fragili</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
